mode: "100644"
text: "# Post types, replies + two worked examples\n\n## Native post types (in rough 2026 order of favor)\n| Type | When | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Long-form single post (Premium) | a real insight/argument | now often out-distributes threads |\n| Native video (<60s) | demo, hot take, BTS | heavily pushed; keep watch-time high |\n| Contestable take / question | spark replies | end on something worth arguing |\n| Image / data-viz | proof, contrast | ~2× text engagement |\n| Article (long-form) | depth | now boosted (native, not external) |\n| Thread | genuine narrative arc | use `thread-writer`; not the default |\n| Poll | contested question | high engagement, weaker follow conversion |\n\n**Link rule:** keep external links **out of the main post** → put the link in the **first reply**.\n\n## The reply strategy (the afterburner)\n- ~**60%** replies on **accounts larger than you** in your niche · ~30% peers · ~10% smaller.\n- Reply **early** to fresh posts from big accounts (be in the first wave); add a genuinely useful or\n  contrarian point — not \"great post\". Standout replies get surfaced to that post's engaged audience.\n- **Quote-post** to add your angle (one sentence of original insight minimum). Never copy-paste.\n\n## The first-hour routine\nPost in your audience's online window → reply to your own first replies immediately → spend ~20–30 min\nreplying into 2–3 bigger conversations in your niche → check back at 60 min. Velocity in this window\ndecides out-of-network reach.\n\n## Expertise-moment play\nWhen news breaks in your niche, post a **fast, informed, opinionated take** with a clear POV and a\nreply hook. These get picked up in For You, spike follows, and attract collaborations. (Pair\n`trend-jacking` for the moment, `ai-search-optimization` for evergreen discoverability.)\n\n## Worked example 1 — contestable long-form (blunt indie-founder voice)\n```\nPOST (long-form, no link): \"Most 'post daily' advice is wrong for X. I posted 3x/day for a month and\ngrew nothing. Then I cut to 1 post + 20 replies a day on bigger accounts in my niche — and tripled\nreach. Replies are the algorithm. Posting is just the bait. Here's the exact split I use: ...\"\nREPLY 1 (link): \"Full breakdown + the 60/30/10 split → [link]\"\nTIMING: 9am audience window; engage every reply for the first hour.\n```\n\n## Worked example 2 — expertise moment (warm studio voice)\n```\nTRIGGER: a tax-rule change trends.\nPOST (native, contestable): \"The new threshold change everyone's panicking about? For most freelancers\nit barely matters -- here's the one number that actually does, and the rule we give every client.\"\nHOOK: ends inviting \"ask me your situation 👇\" (drives author-reply chains = ~150× a like)\nFOLLOW: answer replies personally; quote the best question with the full answer. Link to the guide in a reply.\n```\n\nBoth: read brand-profile + voice-builder first; native + contestable; link in reply; first-hour\nengagement; replies into bigger niche accounts; verified facts. Threads → `thread-writer`; schedule\nposts via `scheduling-and-queue → WoopSocial`; live replies are human.\n"
